        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What makes a facade '3D' rather than just textured paint?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "A textured paint finish creates fine surface roughness visible mainly up close, and a printed or embossed panel pattern only mimics depth visually. True 3D elevation panels have real physical relief, typically ranging from a few millimetres to several centimetres of projection, which is what produces the strong shadow lines that make these facades look different at different times of day as sunlight moves across them."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Where should 3D textured panels be used on a house for the best effect?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Three-dimensional panels deliver the most visual impact when used with intention rather than spread uniformly across an entire building. A single feature wall, often flanking the main entrance or a double-height living area, is one of the most effective and cost-efficient applications. Entrance canopies and porch ceilings are another strong application since visitors naturally look up while approaching."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What material is best for 3D elevation panels?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Aluminium is by far the most common material because it can be precision cut, folded and formed into complex geometric shapes while remaining lightweight, and it accepts durable coatings such as PVDF that hold colour for 15 to 30 years. Stainless steel is used for a more reflective, jewel-like finish, while copper and brass are occasionally used where a warm, evolving patina is part of the design intent."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How much do 3D textured facade panels cost in India?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Simpler fluted or ribbed 3D patterns typically start around ₹900 to ₹1,500 per square foot installed. More complex geometric patterns, such as pyramid or fold panels, generally range from ₹1,200 to ₹2,000 per square foot. Fully custom parametric systems, including coin and sequin patterns, commonly range from ₹1,500 to ₹2,500 per square foot or more, reflecting both design complexity and precision fabrication."
          }
        }
